{{Quote|Tatooine is a worthless rock. Sell the Wookiee back to the gladiators.|translated=1|The Hutt sister, to Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 3" />}}
A '''Hutt''' [[Gender|female]] alongside her [[twin]] [[Unidentified Hutt brother|brother]], attempted to claim [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]'s criminal empire after the death of [[Bib Fortuna]].

==Biography==
Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the [[Gender|female]] [[Hutt]] and her [[Unidentified Hutt brother|brother]] met with [[Boba Fett]] outside of the [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]] in an attempt to make their claim for Jabba's criminal empire.<ref name="Chapter 2" /> Afterwards they sent [[Krrsantan]] to [[Assassination attempt on Boba Fett|kill]] Boba Fett, although they failed. The following day the Twins arrived in [[Boba Fett's Palace]] to apologize for the assassination attempt and they gave him a [[Boba's rancor|rancor]]. Eventually she and her brother left Tatooine after they learned Jabba's territory was promised to the [[Pyke Syndicate]] by [[Mayor of Mos Espa|Mayor]] [[Mok Shaiz]].<ref name="Chapter 3">{{BOBF|Chapter 3: The Streets of Mos Espa}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|You've upset my sister. I'm more patient than she is.|translated=1|The Hutt brother, to Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 2" />}}
According to her brother, this female Hutt was less patient and was upset by Fett's refusal to obey them.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:HuttTwins-TBoBFPoster.png|thumb|right|200px|The Twins character poster for ''The Book of Boba Fett''.]]
The Hutt sister first appeared in the episode "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]]" of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''<ref name="Chapter 2" /> on [[January 5]], [[2022]].<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine release date">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-january-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in January 2022}}</ref> According to the [[Wikipedia:Simplified Chinese|Simplified]] and [[Wikipedia:Traditional Chinese|Traditional Chinese]] subtitles of the episode on Disney+, the female Hutt is the male Hutt's younger sister ([[Wiktionary:妹妹|妹妹]], mèimei). The line is spoken in Huttese, regardless of the language a viewer chooses for audio.<ref name="Chapter 2 Mandarin subs">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}} {{C|simplied and traditional Chinese subtitles}}</ref>

In an interview with [[Wikipedia:TVLine|''TVLine'']], [[Ming-Na Wen]] and [[Temuera Morrison]] revealed that cardboard cutouts were used on set to represent the Hutts that would eventually be realized through computer-generated imagery. Morrison also stated that his stand-in, [[JJ Dashnaw]] or "Jimmy," provided dialogue for the Twins during filming.<ref name="TVLine Hutt Secrets">{{YouTube|video=MHXH73CHK2g|text='Book of Boba Fett' &#124; Temuera Morrison and Ming-Na Wen Talk Episode 2, Hutt Secrets, More|channel=UCL4NqoTi6xcQT4IzUzBwsLg|name=TVLine}}</ref>

